# Maralen, Fae Ascendant: "you may cast a spell ... from among cards exiled with Maralen this turn without paying its mana cost"
# is an alternative cost (CR 118.9); an additional cost is still paid (CR 118.8, 601.2f), with mana of the types it asks for
# - the permission says nothing of mana of any type (CR 609.4b). Bot1 has Llanowar Elves out from turn 1 and casts Maralen on
# turn 3 (Mox Emerald, Mox Sapphire, Black Lotus's three Black): two Elves and Faeries, and Maralen's trigger exiles Bot2's
# Tear Asunder (mana value 2) and Mountain. With {R}{W} floating, Tear Asunder is cast kicked for nothing: the {W} pays the
# kicker's {1}, the {R} can't pay its {B}, so Mox Jet's {B} does, and the {R} is left. Kicked, it exiles the Elves, a nonland
# permanent that is no artifact or enchantment. (Bot2 discarded an Island to hand size on turn 2.)

